==============================================================================
 CONTRAST: finite vs infinite family
==============================================================================
   rho_j over Z_7-cores: FINITE family (2^7) -> inf = MIN = 4cos^2(3pi/7) = 0.19806 (PROVED, THM-590, attained at the doublet).
   R'   over coverings : INFINITE family    -> scan only UPPER-bounds the true inf; inf is the m_R->0 CUSP LIMIT.
   The 2-adic descent FINITIZES R' into rho_j (infinite -> finite); that finitization is what makes the infimum PROVABLE.
